values ('5c1a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'what-if-earth-stopped-spinning', 'What If the Earth Stopped Spinning for One Second?', 'A physics thriller in ten minutes', 'what-if', 'English', 'YouTube Long-form', 10, 1480, 499, 4999, true, 'The equator moves at roughly 1,670 km/h. Freeze it for one second and everything not bolted to bedrock keeps going. A tightly paced explainer that escalates from coffee cups to oceans, with on-screen cues and B-roll notes for every beat.', '## [00:00] HOOK
(VISUAL: slow push-in on a coffee cup on a desk, steam rising)
Right now, while you sit perfectly still, you are moving at about sixteen hundred kilometres an hour. You can''t feel it, because everything around you is moving with you. The desk. The air. The coffee.
Now imagine the planet stops. Not slows down. Stops. For one single second.
The ground halts. You don''t.

## [00:35] SETUP
(VISUAL: globe with a glowing line along the equator, speed counter ticking)
Earth spins once every twenty-four hours. At the equator that means covering roughly forty thousand kilometres a day. Faster than a passenger jet. Faster than the speed of sound.', array['physics', 'earth', 'space', 'hypothetical']::text[], true, true, 214, 4.9, '2026-11-08T10:00:00.000Z')
