## [00:25] THE PIGEON BOX
(VISUAL: archival-style illustration of a pigeon pecking a lever)
In the 1950s, psychologist B. F. Skinner noticed something strange. If a pigeon got food every time it pecked a lever, it pecked steadily. But if food arrived unpredictably, it pecked like it was obsessed.', array['psychology', 'social media', 'habits', 'dopamine']::text[], true, true, 341, 4.9, '2026-10-06T10:00:00.000Z')
