insert into public.script_contents (script_id, body) values ('5c1a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', '## [00:00] HOOK
(VISUAL: thumb flicking up a phone screen, sped up)
You opened this app to check one thing. That was twenty minutes ago.
You''re not weak. You''re not lazy. You''re responding exactly the way a very old experiment predicted you would.

## [00:25] THE PIGEON BOX
(VISUAL: archival-style illustration of a pigeon pecking a lever)
In the 1950s, psychologist B. F. Skinner noticed something strange. If a pigeon got food every time it pecked a lever, it pecked steadily. But if food arrived unpredictably, it pecked like it was obsessed.

## [01:30] VARIABLE REWARDS
(VISUAL: slot machine reels morphing into a social feed)
Skinner called it a variable ratio schedule. You don''t know which pull pays off, so you keep pulling. Slot machines work the same way.

## [03:00] PULL TO REFRESH
(VISUAL: finger pulling down, spinner, new posts)
Pull down, wait, see what you got. Maybe something great. Maybe nothing. That uncertainty is the hook.

## [05:30] INFINITE FEED
(VISUAL: a bottomless page)
A book has chapters. A TV episode ends. A feed doesn''t. Without a natural stopping point, the decision to stop is entirely on you.

## [08:00] RETENTION HOOK
But here''s what most videos on this topic get wrong...

## [10:00] WHAT ACTUALLY HELPS
(VISUAL: phone in greyscale, a drawer closing)
Create stopping points. Turn off non-essential notifications. Move apps off your home screen. Small friction beats big willpower.

## [11:30] OUTRO
You didn''t lose to your phone. You lost to a design. Now you know how it works.') on conflict (script_id) do update set body = excluded.body;
