insert into public.script_contents (script_id, body) values ('5c1a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', '## [00:00] COLD OPEN
(VISUAL: snow blowing across a dark slope, wind audio only)
February 1959. The northern Ural Mountains. A tent sits half-buried in snow on the slope of a mountain the local Mansi people call Kholat Syakhl.
The tent has been cut open. From the inside.
Nearby, footprints lead downhill. Some are in socks. Some are barefoot. In temperatures far below freezing.

## [00:45] THE GROUP
(VISUAL: black-and-white group photo, slow pan across faces)
There were nine of them, led by a twenty-three-year-old engineering student named Igor Dyatlov. They were experienced hikers.

## [02:00] THE SEARCH
(VISUAL: search party in snow, 1959)
When the group failed to send word, search teams went out. They found the tent first, then the bodies, some near a cedar tree, others months later in a ravine.

## [05:00] THE EVIDENCE
(VISUAL: evidence board, handwritten notes)
Some victims had severe internal injuries. Some were barely dressed. The official conclusion in 1959 cited "a compelling natural force."

## [08:00] THE THEORIES
(VISUAL: list animation)
Over the decades: avalanche, katabatic winds, military tests, even the absurd. Most require no conspiracy at all.

## [11:00] 2021: THE SLAB AVALANCHE
(VISUAL: snow simulation)
In 2021, researchers published a model showing how a small, delayed slab avalanche could explain the tent damage and the injuries, triggered by the cut into the slope and wind-blown snow.

## [13:30] WHAT WE ACTUALLY KNOW
Nine people made a desperate decision in the dark. Whatever happened, they were trying to survive.
(MUSIC: single sustained note, fade)') on conflict (script_id) do update set body = excluded.body;
