values ('5c1a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'how-amul-beat-global-giants', 'How Amul Beat the Global Giants', 'A cooperative, a cartoon girl and Operation Flood', 'business-finance', 'English', 'YouTube Long-form', 12, 1690, 649, 6499, true, 'From the 1946 farmers'' strike in Anand to the Amul girl''s topical ads, a brand-strategy story with clear business lessons. Great for business-breakdown channels.', '## [00:00] HOOK
(VISUAL: Amul-style hoarding with a topical pun, then cut to a dairy farm)
The biggest food brand in India isn''t owned by a billionaire. It isn''t owned by a multinational.
It''s owned by millions of farmers, many of whom own just a few cows.
This is how a cooperative from a small town in Gujarat out-competed the world.

## [00:30] ANAND, 1946
(VISUAL: archival-style footage of milk cans, village roads)
In the 1940s, dairy farmers in Kaira district sold their milk through middlemen who set the price.', array['business', 'brand story', 'india', 'amul']::text[], false, true, 129, 4.8, '2026-10-11T10:00:00.000Z')
