insert into public.script_contents (script_id, body) values ('5c1a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', '## [00:00] HOOK
(VISUAL: Amul-style hoarding with a topical pun, then cut to a dairy farm)
The biggest food brand in India isn''t owned by a billionaire. It isn''t owned by a multinational.
It''s owned by millions of farmers, many of whom own just a few cows.
This is how a cooperative from a small town in Gujarat out-competed the world.

## [00:30] ANAND, 1946
(VISUAL: archival-style footage of milk cans, village roads)
In the 1940s, dairy farmers in Kaira district sold their milk through middlemen who set the price.

## [01:30] THE STRIKE
(VISUAL: milk cans lined up, unsold)
Farmers, encouraged by leaders like Tribhuvandas Patel and with support from Sardar Patel, refused to sell to middlemen. They formed their own cooperative in 1946.

## [03:30] KURIEN ARRIVES
(VISUAL: young engineer stepping off a bus)
Verghese Kurien, an engineer, joined and helped turn the cooperative into a modern dairy operation.

## [06:00] OPERATION FLOOD
(VISUAL: map of India filling with milk-drop icons)
The Anand model became national through Operation Flood, launched in 1970, which helped make India the world''s largest milk producer.

## [08:30] THE AMUL GIRL
(VISUAL: topical hoardings over the decades)
Since 1966, the polka-dot-dress Amul girl has commented on the news with puns. Cheap, fast, beloved.

## [10:30] LESSONS
Own the supply chain. Keep the farmer in the profit. Build a brand people quote.

## [11:30] OUTRO
The giant isn''t one company. It''s millions of farmers who decided to stop being small.') on conflict (script_id) do update set body = excluded.body;
